                        "username": "chandramohan83"
                    },
                    "message": "I think you misunderstood this MR.\n\nThis predefined group can't be removed dynamically\n\nconstexpr std::array<const char*, 4> predefinedGroups = {\n    \"redfish\", \"ipmi\", \"ssh\", \"hostconsole\"}; \n\nif you want to remove any group that is only possible statically not dynamically \nfrom this group.\n\nThis MR checks this predefined groups are present in \"/etc/group\" if not present then it creates entry in \"/etc/group\" that's all.\n\nfor IPMI, I use meson option to define two predfined groups example\n\n#if IPMI_ENABLED\npredfined group with IPMI \n#else\nIPMI not present in the predfined group.\n#endif"
                },
                {
